{"id":"fujifilm_eterna_cp_3513di","name":"Fujifilm Eterna-CP 3513DI","manufacturer":"Fujifilm","kind":"Cine negative","isBlackAndWhite":false,"source":"Negs","targetPrint":null,"datasheet":null,"credit":"Copyright (c) 2026 Noah Haasis (Negs preparation). Method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Measurement data (c) FUJIFILM Corporation.","license":"Negs film profile, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Prepared with the profile-creation method of spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm; profiles CC BY-SA 4.0, see SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt). Derivatives must credit both, note their modifications and remain CC BY-SA 4.0. Changes: data/CHANGELOG.txt.","dataSource":"Prepared for Negs from the manufacturer's brochure: FUJICOLOR POSITIVE FILM ETERNA-CP 3513DI/3613DI brochure, Ref. No. KB-505E, (c) 2005 FUJIFILM Corporation, PDF page 1 (spectral sensitivity, per-dye spectral density, characteristic curves). PDF sha256 ce5f63f622dc2024557b4c1f0ec018efdc0c0426eb00c3348629c05d30dfaf74. Data (c) FUJIFILM Corporation. The curves were read from the PDF's vector paths (tools/film_profiles/extract_pdf.py); the points and axis calibration are in data/profile-sources/fujifilm-print/fujifilm_eterna_cp_3513di/.\nMethod: spektrafilm's public-era profile creator by Andrea Volpato (commit b2c7fe6), its steps for papers and print films: D-min removed (base synthesised from the curves' D-min), log E zero where green is 0.735 over D-min, Fujifilm's own per-dye spectra scaled so equal amounts view as an 18.4 % neutral under the viewing illuminant (K75P), status-A unmixing, a 3 norm_cdfs curve fit, densitometer normalisation. Then the author's print normalisation (spektrafilm #557): sensitivities scaled so the TH-KG3 enlarger lamp through Y50 M50 and the mid-scale neutral of kodak_vision3_250d gives raw exposure 1 per channel. Negs step before the unmixing: each status-A curve moved along log E so log E 0 develops the metameric neutral's status-A density (the private creator's preliminary neutral shift; R +0.165, G -0.033, B +0.074 log E). Calibration: the same steps rebuild Kodak 2383 and 2393 from spektrafilm's public raw data to within CIEDE2000 0.9-1.0 mean (2.6 at most) of the shipped profiles on a ColorChecker printed from cine negatives, and their neutral filters within about 3 CC (data/profile-sources/fujifilm-print/calibration/). Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md D12.\nBrochure specifics: the characteristic curves' log H axis is unlabelled (one square is 0.5 log H), and green and blue are plotted 1.0 and 2.0 log H to the left of red; the shift is undone, and the pre-alignment fixes each channel's position anyway. Fujifilm draws each dye curve with the film base under it (where all four are drawn, Y + M + C - Gray = 2 x base). The base taken off is the one this brochure's own dye chart implies, smoothed 20 nm. Undrawn parts filled: yellow 685-695 nm from the Gray curve less the other two dyes and the base. Sensitivity is drawn only near each peak (red in two pieces, 360-442 nm and 630-723 nm): beyond each drawn end it continues with the shape of kodak_2383 (Kodak's ECP-2 print film, the calibration stock), joined at the end and only falling away from it. Share of the normalisation's raw exposure from these tails: R 12%, G 1%, B 0% (red: mostly 600-640 nm, where an orange-masked negative passes the most light).\nChecks: curve fit within 0.015 D; status-A remix within 0.031 D of the brochure's curves up to D 2.0 and 0.089 D above; raw exposure 1 per channel through the reference film.\nNegs choices: reference illuminant TH-KG3 and viewing illuminant K75P, use 'cine' and antihalation 'strong', as the shipped spektrafilm Kodak 2383; log_sensitivity_density_over_min 1.0 as printed (reciprocal of exposure (erg/cm2) for density 1.0 above minimum density); spectra left empty (null) outside 400-695 nm for the dyes; characteristic curves in log10 H. Printed as 2854K tungsten, 1/100 s, Fuji SC-41 + CC-90Y + CC-60M; ECP-2B.\nRecorded exceptions: characteristic x axis (relative): Exposure [log H] carries no numbers, only a 0.5 log H scale bar spanning one grid square; the offset is arbitrary (log E 0 is set by step 2 and the neutral pre-alignment) and the scale is 0.5 log H per square.","referenceIlluminant":"TH-KG3","densitometer":"status_A","densityMinimum":[0.084,0.1,0.142],"wavelengths":[380,385,390,395,400,405,410,415,420,425,430,435,440,445,450,455,460,465,470,475,480,485,490,495,500,505,510,515,520,525,530,535,540,545,550,555,560,565,570,575,580,585,590,595,600,605,610,615,620,625,630,635,640,645,650,655,660,665,670,675,680,685,690,695,700,705,710,715,720,725,730,735,740,745,750,755,760,765,770,775,780],"logSensitivity":[[0.36216,0.14566,0.49579],[0.28641,0.036514,0.40017],[0.2122,-0.087567,0.28543],[0.13776,-0.18473,0.15724],[0.050125,-0.25111,0.074853],[-0.049117,-0.33801,0.060722],[-0.1573,-0.48726,0.083207],[-0.27272,-0.66809,0.13946],[-0.40083,-0.85267,0.2189],[-0.56415,-0.94464,0.30451],[-0.73391,-0.93906,0.39448],[-0.89469,-0.89508,0.48898],[-1.0358,-0.83728,0.57775],[-1.1925,-0.74443,0.62311],[-1.3763,-0.65255,0.69162],[-1.5562,-0.55879,0.82208],[-1.7306,-0.45649,0.99413],[-1.8979,-0.34923,1.2047],[-2.0565,-0.23091,1.3991],[-2.2048,-0.16416,1.3513],[-2.3411,-0.11691,1.0262],[-2.4638,-0.059389,0.59473],[-2.5713,0.015814,0.082912],[-2.662,0.099494,-0.32748],[-2.7343,0.18286,-0.67936],[-2.7866,0.24768,-0.96721],[-2.8173,0.27314,-1.3993],[-2.825,0.2751,-1.8893],[-2.8327,0.27739,-2.3443],[-2.8634,0.29,-2.7679],[-2.9154,0.36815,-3.1633],[-2.987,0.48116,-3.5332],[-3.0758,0.65845,-3.8799],[-3.1791,0.79052,-4.2056],[-3.2917,0.86702,-4.5122],[-3.4028,0.68792,-4.8013],[-3.4862,0.26515,-5.0743],[-3.4871,-0.17806,-5.3325],[-3.3394,-0.62685,-5.5772],[-3.0355,-1.0339,-5.8093],[-2.625,-1.2816,-6.0298],[-2.1278,-1.6334,-6.2395],[-1.6446,-1.9739,-6.4393],[-1.5784,-2.2986,-6.6297],[-1.5523,-2.6085,-6.8115],[-1.485